# sabotage=RopesPassForFlatStrings: every string passes for the result of FlattenString, so the characters of a rope are read as if the rope were flat. The run stops in front of the read, and names the operation
# FORM: AsRead
# RUN: run-in-shell globalThis.argumentCount = 2;
# REQUIRES: not-windows
# OPTIONS: disable=pass:InlineCalls,pass:InlineHeads testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime sabotage=RopesPassForFlatStrings
# CHECK: AOT validation: OperationPreconditionBroken f
# PROGRAM-OF: ropes-pass-for-flat-strings-left-alone.ir
